## Context

Child of master ticket 0660. Current zoteus artifacts call the configuration
default while disclosing a harness-supplied `ZOTEUS_TRANSFORMERS_PATH` pointing
at a preinstalled runtime. That changes cold-start behavior. Separately,
`R10-local-by-default` fails a target reporting no embedder even though no
embedder alone cannot cause text to leave the machine. This child owns faithful
default setup and accurate placement of the local-embedder mechanism check.

## Actions

- Define the ordinary-user default from shipped configuration and installation
  behavior, with every harness input compared against it.
- Run the cold default without a preinstalled runtime override, plus a disclosed
  warm repeat; prove whether acquisition, fallback and status disclosure occur.
- Refuse the label `default` when any non-default input affects the behavior
  under test. A necessary harness deviation gets its own configuration class.
- Re-home or rename the local-active-embedder check so it states the mechanism
  it proves. Do not score `locality: none` as R10 exfiltration absent a ruling
  that changes the promise.

## Test

- [ ] A planted runtime override makes the default-premise guard fail.
- [ ] Cold and warm controls prove cache state rather than trusting a path.
- [ ] Local, remote, absent and undisclosed locality states remain distinct.
- [ ] A local embedder beside an independent exfiltrator cannot make R10 green.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Real-target R10 evidence is taken under a verified ordinary-user default,
      or labeled as a distinct non-default configuration.
- [ ] The local-embedder check no longer claims more than its observation.
- [ ] Default-premise and locality-state controls have been seen red/green as
      appropriate.
- [ ] README standing cites only evidence taken under the configuration it names.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass.
